                <pb facs="0150" n="78" sameAs="frus:frus1865p4/pg78"/>

                <head>Fraternity of the People Lodge</head>
                <dateline>
                    <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-volume-rules" calendar="gregorian"
                        notAfter="1865-07-31T23:59:59+00:09" notBefore="1865-04-15T00:00:00+00:09"
                        >undated</date>
                </dateline>
                <note rend="inline" rendition="#center" type="source">[Translation.]</note>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Address of the Lodge of the Fraternity of the People, in
                        the east of Paris, to the American Free Masons, on the occasion of the death
                        of Mr. Lincoln</hi>.</p>
                <p>The Loge la Fraternité des Peuples has profoundly felt the great grief which has
                    agitated the world on the receipt of the news of the horrible outrage to which
                    F** Lincoln has fallen a victim. F** of America, the masons of France <pb
                        facs="0151" n="79" xml:id="pg79"/> lament the irreparable loss of the
                    virtuous citizen, of the great politician; but they know that with them and by
                    them slavery will be annihilated, and that the sacred cause of liberty will
                    shine forth in a great triumph which is at hand, a glorious compensation for the
                    deep grief of this sad period.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>E. DENISE, </signed>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Ven</hi>. **.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
